CALL newPutForth(400, 1, 'Every problem the government touches becomes more complicated and more expensive. The best thing Washington can do for most issues is step aside and let Americans handle it.');
CALL newPutForth(401, 1, 'Free market has done more to lift people out of poverty than any government program in history. Look at Eastern Europe after 1989, China after Deng. Markets work — government doesn\'t.');
CALL newPutForth(403, 1, 'Good governance means limited governance — small, transparent, accountable government that does what the Constitution authorizes: defense, courts, basic infrastructure. Nothing more.');
CALL newPutForth(404, 1, 'Federal regulatory code is over 180,000 pages. Nobody\'s read it. Half probably contradicts the other half. Congress should repeal two regulations for every new one it adds. Every year.');
CALL newPutForth(405, 1, 'Name one federal agency that\'s ever been abolished. Can\'t? That\'s because bureaucracies never die — they just grow, hire more people, and find new reasons to justify their existence.');
CALL newPutForth(406, 1, 'Name a time in history when a government voluntarily limited its own power. Can\'t. Power is self-perpetuating. It always seeks more. The Constitution\'s checks exist because the Founders knew this.');
CALL newPutForth(407, 1, 'Washington is already too big — $35 trillion in debt, 180,000 pages of regulation, agencies that haven\'t been reviewed in decades. Time to actually fight back and cut the thing down.');
CALL newPutForth(409, 1, 'Show me a government bureaucracy and I\'ll show you corruption. DMV to the Pentagon — when there\'s no competition and no accountability, inefficiency and graft are inevitable outcomes.');
CALL newPutForth(410, 1, 'Nobody reads the tax code because it\'s 75,000 pages — and that\'s intentional. Complexity protects the bureaucrats. A regulation should be simple enough for a normal person to understand.');
CALL newPutForth(411, 1, 'What good is a regulation nobody enforces? Half our rules are paper rules because there aren\'t enough inspectors and penalties are too weak. Write fewer rules, enforce them better.');
CALL newPutForth(412, 1, 'Government doesn\'t earn its budget — it just takes it. No profits, no losses, no accountability. Every serious study of government vs. private efficiency reaches the same conclusion.');
CALL newPutForth(447, 1, 'Look out for your neighbor. That\'s what real community is built on — not government programs, but people giving a damn about the person next door. We\'ve forgotten how to do that.');
CALL newPutForth(564, 1, 'Legitimate government only exists by consent of the governed. That\'s the American idea. When government stops representing the people who created it, it loses its claim to authority.');
CALL newPutForth(565, 1, 'Sovereignty belongs to the people — not to Washington bureaucrats, not to unelected regulators, not to international bodies. The people are the ultimate source of legitimate authority.');
CALL newPutForth(566, 1, 'Every time government \'solves\' a problem and makes it worse, the answer is always more spending on the same failed approach. That\'s not progress — that\'s a protection racket.');
CALL newPutForth(570, 1, 'Constitutional republic — that\'s what we built. Not a pure democracy, not a technocracy. Elected representatives, accountable to voters, bounded by the Constitution. That\'s the design.');
CALL newPutForth(668, 1, 'County government, township government, water district, school board — every layer takes a cut of your taxes. Consolidate or eliminate the overlap. Too many bureaucracies chasing the same dollar.');
CALL newPutForth(669, 1, 'No reason the same territory should have two complete sets of administrators, two HR departments, two pension systems. Consolidate city and county. It\'s waste, plain and simple.');
CALL newPutForth(670, 1, 'A small state with 50,000 people doesn\'t need three tiers of local government. One accountable body, clear jurisdiction, no bureaucratic overlap. That\'s efficient government.');
CALL newPutForth(671, 1, 'Government should be exactly as large as the job requires — not one person more. Every additional layer is another opportunity for waste, corruption, and losing sight of the mission.');
CALL newPutForth(689, 1, 'Road to hell is paved with good intentions. Every bloated government program started with a good idea. Then bureaucrats showed up, created fiefdoms, and the original mission was forgotten.');
CALL newPutForth(706, 1, 'National defense, interstate highways, flood control — yes, some things require collective action beyond what individuals can handle. That\'s what government is actually for. Short list.');
CALL newPutForth(707, 1, 'Courts, military, police — those jobs require public authority and legal accountability that a private citizen doesn\'t have. Government belongs there. Not in healthcare or education.');
CALL newPutForth(708, 1, 'Take the law into your own hands and you\'re judge, jury, and executioner with no oversight. That\'s not justice — that\'s chaos. Courts exist for a reason. Self-defense is different.');
CALL newPutForth(920, 1, 'Head Start, DARE, ethanol mandates, Cash for Clunkers — the government\'s program hall of shame. Studies proved they didn\'t work. Kept running them anyway because someone\'s job depended on it.');
CALL newPutForth(1045, 1, 'Saw regulations at the mill that cost $10 million in compliance costs to mitigate $100,000 in risk. Happens constantly. Washington imposes the burden without ever running a cost-benefit analysis.');
CALL newPutForth(1049, 1, 'Regulations written in 1972 are still on the books. Technology changed, risks changed, the whole industry changed — but the rule stays because nobody made time to review it. That\'s the job.');
CALL newPutForth(1050, 1, 'One agency says the product is safe, the next says it\'s dangerous. One administration rolls back rules, the next reinstates them. Industry can\'t plan or invest. That\'s your government.');
CALL newPutForth(1051, 1, 'Filed a comment with OSHA once. Two years later got a letter saying they\'d \'consider\' our concerns. By then we\'d already changed the process. Government responds to the last crisis, not yours.');
CALL newPutForth(1052, 1, 'System rewards dysfunction — spend your whole budget or lose it next year. Write ten rules to cover every edge case. Hire more staff to justify the department. America can do better than this.');
CALL newPutForth(1053, 1, 'Government should work for the people who live under it, not for the bureaucrats who administer it. We need structural reform — fewer agencies, clearer rules, real accountability for failure.');
